  <note>
    <title>Trust the GPG key for the Package Hub repository</title>
    <para>
    If you select the Package Hub add-on and see a popup, trust the GPG key for that repository.
    </para>
  </note>
  <section xml:id="reference-deployment-manual-software-desktop">
    <title>Select a desktop</title>
    <para>
      Select a desktop environment to get a graphical interface. &productname; shops with the
      &gnome; desktop. <!-- You can install other desktop environments like KDE or Xfce, if you enable
      the &ph; (see <xref linkend="reference-deployment-manual-registration-extensions"/>). -->
    </para>
  </section>
  <section xml:id="reference-deployment-manual-software-patterns">
    <title>Additional software patterns</title>
    <para>
      Patterns are curated sets of packages for common use cases and features to extent the system.
      The default installation includes <literal>Kernel dump tooling</literal> and
      <literal>&selnx; support</literal>. To remove them or install additional patterns, click
      <guimenu>Change patterns</guimenu>.
    </para>
  </section>
